course: dictionary
lesson: 11516
title: Algae: tiny green living things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Algae are simple, plant-like living things. They grow in water or damp places, and most are green, brown or red. Like plants, they make their own food from sunlight. «The pond had a thick layer of algae on top.»
explain: Some algae are so small that you could never see one alone. Others are big, like seaweeds, which are large algae that grow in the sea. The clue is in the word «large», so you can tell that algae come in many sizes.
explain: You may know algae as the green slime on ponds, rocks, fish tanks and swimming pools. Read the words around it: «The rocks by the lake were covered in slippery green algae.» Slippery and covered tell you that algae can make things unsafe to walk on.
explain: Algae are very important. Tiny creatures in the water eat them, and they give off much of the oxygen we breathe. But be careful: some algae in lakes can be poisonous to people and dogs, so always obey warning signs.
fact: Algae are simple, plant-like living things that usually grow in water or damp places.
fact: Most algae are green, brown or red, and they make their own food from sunlight.
fact: «Algae» is the plural word; one of them is called an «alga», but that word is rarely used.
fact: Seaweeds are large algae.
fact: Blue-green algae in some lakes can be poisonous to people and dogs, so obey warning signs.
exercise: «The pond was covered in green algae.» What are algae? | *Simple plant-like living things that grow in water | A type of hard rock | A metal used in pipes | A kind of fish that lives in ponds
exercise: «The rocks were slippery with algae, so we walked very carefully.» Why did they walk carefully? | The rocks were hot from the sun | *The algae made the rocks slippery | The rocks were very tall | The algae made the rocks sing
exercise: Seaweeds are large algae. What does this tell you about seaweed? | It is a dry plant from the desert | It is a metal | *It is a large, plant-like living thing that grows in water | It is a kind of bird
test: What do most algae use to make their own food? | Sugar from the shop | *Sunlight | Soil from the ground | Food from other animals
test: Why should you obey warning signs near a lake with green scum? | Algae are sweet to taste | *Some algae in lakes can be poisonous to people and dogs | Warning signs are only for fish | Warning signs show where to swim fastest
exam: Tiny creatures eat algae, and algae give off much of the oxygen we breathe. Why are algae important? | They are only used to make paint | They are always poisonous to all living things | *They feed tiny creatures and give us oxygen to breathe | They make rocks dry and smooth
